  postAuthor: Prof. Tunde Balogun
  authorImage: {fileID: 0}
  postHeader: 
  postContent: "New research warns that constant exposure to blue light from smartphones
    \u201Ccan lead to irreversible brain damage.\u201D Experts disagree, but daily
    screen time is now being blamed for a range of illnesses.\n"
  funFact_Hint: "Notice whether the story\u2019s main goal is to unsettle you."
  BiasChoices:
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 1
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: "It uses alarming phrases (\u201Cirreversible brain
      damage\u201D) to create panic. "
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 7
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: This bias chooses which topics to cover; this piece
      is trying to scare you.
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 8
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: "Confirmation bias cherry-picks supporting data;
      here it simply emphasizes worst-case scenarios. \n"
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 3
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: 'False balance would present two sides equally;
      here dissenting views are downplayed.

'
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 2
